{
  "evaluation": "All three correctly treat the pair as genuine, identify population as the primary difference, and list outcome measurement as an additional difference. Both studies examine vitamin D levels, and neither provides an explicit underpowering signal that would justify an apparent disagreement. A is strongest because it also acknowledges that Study A establishes an association but not its direction, so the supplied harm label is unsupported. B narrowly outranks C for explicitly explaining the association-versus-null contrast; otherwise their judgments are essentially equivalent.",
  "ranking": ["A", "B", "C"]
}
